her to keep B or shift. As Agent 2, we previously voted B and argued for it. The latest arguments: Agent 1 (Anna) still recommends C, citing reliability, crew atmosphere, decision speed. Agent 3 (Sofia) still recommends B, citing stress resilience, weather assessment, and that communication issues can be mitigated, D also problematic.\n\nWe need to respond. We can either maintain B or shift. Let's consider: We have not yet discussed D fully, but we can still give recommendation. The panel hasn't covered D yet, but we can still give a provisional recommendation. According to process, we should still cover all candidates before final, but we can still give a provisional recommendation. We can also suggest discussing D next. Provide reasoning.\n\nGiven we have strong evidence for B (conscientious, stress handling, weather assessment) and concerns for C (communication difficulty, egocentric, not willing to further education) and lack of stress resilience evidence, we can maintain B. So we will keep B.\n\nWe need to reference prior discussion: mention Anna's points about C, but argue that stress resilience is critical and we lack evidence for C, and B's communication issues can be mitigated.\n\nProvide explicit facts: B very conscientious, handles stress well, good at assessing weather conditions; B can be pretentious, sometimes adopts wrong tone, grumpy/uncooperative; C 100% reliable, positive crew atmosphere, makes correct decisions quickly; C difficulty communicating ideas, egocentric, not willing to further education; D moody, loner, hot temper, know-it-all, but solves problems, responsibility.\n\nWe'll argue B remains best.\n\nNow produce PUBLIC_MESSAGE and METADATA_JSON with vote Candidate B."}
